abstract: >
  A reproducible, ranked, FAIR-indexed research dossier collection of 120 open
  mathematical problems across 38 fields (plus a daily full sidecar mirror of
  all 26 Left to Solve research programs / 62,790 targets), paired with a
  standalone eight-domain, six-kernel Lean 4.35.0 formal verification core with
  autoImplicit = false
  (74 headline theorems, 20 non-vacuity witnesses, and 24 adversarial
  refutations = 118 audited declarations across Collatz Fine-Wilf valuation
  ceilings / chiral sign conjugacy / mod-3 chiral asymmetry / global 3-adic
  cycle exclusion / d <= 7 & unconditional 1-/2-/3-/4-odd-step positive-cycle
  exclusion / sharp intercept & Eliahou-Steiner amplitude bounds / catalytic
  cylinders, Erdos-Straus, full Lonely Runner through n = 3, Brocard through
  n <= 20, Primes/Twin Primes, Goldbach, Complete Euclid-Euler even perfect
  number theorem & Euler 2p | (q-1) Mersenne prime divisor congruence, and exact
  Ramsey R(3,3) = 6 and R(3,4) = 9), a catalytic C17/BMI2 + safe Rust native
  Collatz accelerator & 5-Vector Asymmetric Hydra suite (up to 7,137x speedup,
  4 KiB stack DFS, 500k ASan/UBSan fuzz cases), live negative kernel rejection,
  automated primary-source citation and Crossref/DataCite retraction auditing,
  dual DigiCert RFC 3161 + Bitcoin OpenTimestamps cryptographic manifest proofs,
  a deterministic BM25/dense RAG corpus, RO-Crate 1.1 and Croissant 1.0
  metadata, a compiled AMS-LaTeX white paper, and documented epistemic integrity
  gates. Human contributions (CRediT):
  Conceptualization, Methodology, Supervision, Formal analysis (statement-fidelity
  audit), Validation, Writing - review & editing. AI tools were used as disclosed
  drafting and formalization instruments; all formal theorems are independently
  checked by six Lean 4.35.0 kernels. Not peer-reviewed.
keywords:
  - mathematics
  - open problems
  - conjectures
  - lean4
  - formal verification
  - meta-analysis
  - retrieval-augmented generation
  - knowledge base
